## Scenario context

Domain-Driven Design (DDD) shifts the focus of software development from database schemas to core business logic. By implementing a rich domain model using Entities, Value Objects, and Aggregate Roots, we protect business invariants directly inside our code. This guide contrasts anemic domain models with rich DDD patterns in Java.

